1
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,253
Hi! Welcome to TrainTanmay. I'm going to give you a quick tour,

2
00:00:07,203 --> 00:00:09,790
so you can get the most out of your revision.

3
00:00:10,339 --> 00:00:15,650
TrainTanmay is a set of free revision apps, made by an A level student, for other students.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:21,826
Each world on the start screen is its own app: Design & Technology, Physics, Chemistry,

5
00:00:21,776 --> 00:00:23,108
Maths, and the ESAT.

6
00:00:30,537 --> 00:00:33,687
Just pick a world to jump in. Let's start with Chemistry.

7
00:00:36,559 --> 00:00:40,474
Every app works in a similar way. The home page shows your progress,

8
00:00:40,424 --> 00:00:43,544
the flashcards you've got due, and where you left off.

9
00:00:44,093 --> 00:00:48,779
Along the top, you'll find the notes, practice questions, past papers, and the labs.

10
00:00:49,329 --> 00:00:52,875
To switch apps, tap the TrainTanmay logo in the top corner.

11
00:00:52,825 --> 00:00:56,548
Its colour tells you which app you're in: orange is Chemistry.

12
00:00:57,099 --> 00:01:01,583
Looking for something specific? Use Jump to anything, and just type what you need.

13
00:01:02,132 --> 00:01:07,879
Every topic has full notes with worked examples, plus key terms, equations, flashcards,

14
00:01:07,829 --> 00:01:08,599
and videos.

15
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:12,424
The notes were written with AI, so if anything looks off,

16
00:01:12,374 --> 00:01:15,196
double-check it against your textbook or a video.

17
00:01:15,746 --> 00:01:19,786
The calculation drills give you new numbers every time. Type your answer,

18
00:01:19,736 --> 00:01:22,737
and it's marked straight away, with a worked solution.

19
00:01:23,288 --> 00:01:27,863
And in the labs, you can spin real 3D molecules, see every bond angle,

20
00:01:27,813 --> 00:01:30,448
then flip it into an exam-style drawing.

21
00:01:31,718 --> 00:01:36,933
Design & Technology covers the whole Edexcel Product Design course. Flip a flashcard,

22
00:01:36,883 --> 00:01:41,065
then say whether you knew it, and it'll come back at the right time.

23
00:01:41,517 --> 00:01:45,782
Physics has notes, practice tests, and nearly fifty labs, like this one,

24
00:01:45,732 --> 00:01:47,656
which flies real space missions.

25
00:01:48,119 --> 00:01:53,063
In Maths, you can search thousands of past papers, topic packs and worksheets,

26
00:01:53,013 --> 00:01:55,008
all sorted by course and topic.

27
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:59,528
And the ESAT app has real admissions test questions, timed mocks,

28
00:01:59,478 --> 00:02:04,795
and analytics that show your weak spots. Plus a few games, for when you need a break.

29
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:10,064
Your progress saves automatically, right here in your browser. You don't need an account.

30
00:02:10,614 --> 00:02:15,528
From Save progress, you can download a backup file, and load it again on any device.

31
00:02:16,077 --> 00:02:20,632
Or, sign in with Google, and your progress follows you to your phone, your laptop,

32
00:02:20,582 --> 00:02:22,006
and your school computer.

33
00:02:22,555 --> 00:02:27,313
Syncing only ever adds progress, so nothing on one device can wipe out another.

34
00:02:30,517 --> 00:02:35,329
Now for the fun part. Study leagues are weekly leaderboards, for you and your friends.

35
00:02:35,878 --> 00:02:40,628
They count your active revision minutes, whenever you're clicking, typing or scrolling,

36
00:02:40,578 --> 00:02:41,655
in any of the apps.

37
00:02:42,205 --> 00:02:46,671
Share your league code to invite people. You can be in up to five leagues at once.

38
00:02:48,104 --> 00:02:52,366
Everyone's minutes reset on Monday, so there's a new crown to win every week.

39
00:02:52,915 --> 00:02:56,222
To start your own league, or join a friend's, tap New or join.

40
00:02:58,051 --> 00:03:02,505
Everyone reads differently. Tap the Aa button for a dyslexia-friendly font.

41
00:03:03,054 --> 00:03:08,569
The menu next to it switches the colours. Try dark mode, or a softer, warmer background.

42
00:03:09,119 --> 00:03:13,420
And in the logo menu, you can read everything in Welsh or Scottish Gaelic.

43
00:03:14,083 --> 00:03:19,016
If you spot a mistake, or something's broken, tap Report a bug, and let Tanmay know.

44
00:03:18,966 --> 00:03:19,946
It really helps.

45
00:03:20,495 --> 00:03:24,672
That's everything! Good luck with your revision, and I'll see you on the leaderboard.

